# Khandaq — review ownership for security-critical paths.
#
# KHANDAQ (re-audit 2026-08-22, S-01). A workflow that exists is not a gate; a path that anyone can
# change without a second pair of eyes is not owned. These are the paths where a quiet edit changes
# what the fleet trusts: the push relay and the config that fronts it, the release and provenance
# workflows, the check scripts that are supposed to fail closed, and this file itself.
#
# NOTE ON A SINGLE-MAINTAINER REPOSITORY. GitHub will not let an author approve their own pull
# request, so requiring code-owner APPROVAL here would deadlock the only maintainer. The ruleset
# therefore requires a pull request and green required checks, and CODEOWNERS requests the review
# rather than blocking on it. When a second maintainer exists, turn on
# `require_code_owner_review` in the "Security gates (S-01)" ruleset — that is the one setting that
# has to change, and it is deliberately recorded here rather than left to be rediscovered.

* @UMMAPROJECTS

# Push relay: the only Internet-facing service Khandaq operates.
/infra/push/                @UMMAPROJECTS
/infra/nginx/               @UMMAPROJECTS

# Release, provenance and the supply chain.
/.github/workflows/         @UMMAPROJECTS
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @UMMAPROJECTS
/scripts/ci-*               @UMMAPROJECTS
/scripts/check-*            @UMMAPROJECTS
/scripts/deploy-*           @UMMAPROJECTS
/scripts/verify-*           @UMMAPROJECTS
/scripts/generate-release-manifest.py  @UMMAPROJECTS
/scripts/generate-security-headers.py  @UMMAPROJECTS

# Dependency pinning: changing these changes what the build trusts. witness.gradle is the committed
# list of maven artifact hashes the release build verifies against; bundled-deps.json is the desktop
# inventory the EOL/waiver gate reads.
/khandaq-android-trifa/android-refimpl-app/app/witness.gradle  @UMMAPROJECTS
/khandaq-desktop/buildscripts/bundled-deps.json                @UMMAPROJECTS

# The published security contact and policy.
/SECURITY.md                @UMMAPROJECTS
/web/.well-known/           @UMMAPROJECTS
